  "question": {
    "text": "The displacement of an object of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;given by the relation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> , where <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math> is time in seconds. If the work done by the net force on the object in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>joule</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;are smallest integer values, then what is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></math>?",
    "image": null
  },
